m. The wound was closed with a complex closure. The defect was undermined extensively (1 cm) to reduce tension and distortion of the adjacent structures. Buried absorbable sutures were also used to close the subcutaneous and dermal components of the defect. The wound was approximated utilizing 3-O Vicryl and 3-O Nylon sutures. \nThe final closure size is 6.5 cm. \n Post-Operative:\nThe patient tolerated the procedure well with no complications, and minimal bleeding. The wound was covered with Vaseline and Press Dressing. Detailed oral and written post-operative instructions were reviewed and given to the patient. The patient instructed to remove dressing in 24 hours, sleep with the surgical site elevated this evening, avoid alcohol, trauma and tobacco.\n Patient was informed to return in 2 Weeks for suture removal with Bree Parker PA-C.', 'location': 'Right lower Leg', 'stages': 1}], 'has_closure': True, 'closure_sections': [{'type': 'complex', 'size': 3.7, 'location': 'Mid Scalp', 'location_group': 'extremities', 'group_key': 'complex_extremities', 'text': 'A. Excision Malignant Lesion & Margins\nClinical Diagnosis: Excised Melanoma In Situ\nLocation: Mid Scalp\nMethod: Excision\nLesion Size: 3.1 - 3.0 cm\nExcision Size, including margins: 3.6 x 3.5 cm\nThe patient was evaluated preoperative and noted to be in stable condition. \n Informed consent was obtained from the patient. All risks, benefits, and alternatives regarding the survey have been reviewed in detail with the patient. \n This includes risks of bleeding, infection, scarring recurrence of lesion and need for further procedures. \nAfter consent was obtained, attention was turned toward the area of interest which was disinfected and cleaned with alcohol. Local anesthetic, 2% lidocaine with epinephrine was infiltrated around the site. An elliptical incision with the appropriate margins was made using a Number 15 to obtain a full thickness specimen. Dissection of the surrounding/overlying tissue was perform