ee plane was obtained. \n1st Stage: 2 Sections, Positive\n2nd Stage: 1 Sections, Negative\nPost-Mohs Deficit Size: 1.9 x 1.5 cm.\n Repair Options:\n \n After a discussion of wound management options, \n due to the size and location of the defect, and the need to achieve optimal cosmesis, \n avoid hematoma, the following wound management was agreed upon to provide the best functional and cosmetic result. \n Performed: \n The wound was closed with an Adjacent Tissue Transfer on the same day of mohs. \n Reconstruction:\nRepair: Adjacent Tissue Transfer \nThe postoperative deficit was 1.9 x 1.5 cm. Additional relaxing incisions were made along the wound to develop pedicle skin flaps which were then widely undermined and advanced to close the deficit. The wound was approximated utilizing 4-O Vicryl and 4-O Nylon sutures. \nThe final closure size is 3.1 cm2. \n Post-Operative:\nThe patient tolerated the procedure well with no complications, and minimal bleeding. The wound was covered with Vaseline and Press Dressing. Detailed oral and written post-operative instructions were reviewed and given to the patient. The patient instructed to remove dressing in 24 hours, sleep with the surgical site elevated this evening, avoid alcohol, trauma and tobacco.\n Patient was informed to return in 10 Days with Dora Mora, Np.'}], 'has_srt': False, 'srt_sections': [], 'has_debridement': False, 'debridement_sections': [], 'has_procedure': False, 'closure_aggregated': [{'type': 'adjacent', 'group_key': 'adjacent_critical', 'total_size': 3.1, 'locations': ['Left Nose']}]}
