2026-05-29 14:53:48.253 | INFO     | services.clinical_parser:extract_closure_sections:276 - 📊 FINAL CLOSURES: [{'type': 'intermediate', 'size': 3.0, 'location': 'Mid Back', 'location_group': 'trunk', 'group_key': 'intermediate_trunk', 'text': 'A. Biopsy\nClinical Diagnosis: Dermatofibroma\nLocation: Left Post Shoulder\nMethod: Incisional\nLesion Size: 1.3 - 0.6 cm\n The patient gave informed consent for this procedure. After consent was obtained, attention was turned toward the area of interest which was disinfected and cleaned with alcohol. Local anesthetic, 1% lidocaine with epinephrine was infiltrated around the area of interest. An elliptical incision was made using a Number 15 and part of the lesion was removed. The specimen was placed in a bottle labeled A. #WC20-844. The wound was closed with Simple Closure. The site was closed with simple interrupted sutures.\nPressure was applied to achieve hemostasis. Bacitracin was applied at the wound site and it was bandaged. Patient tolerated the procedure well and wound care instructions were reviewed and given to the patient.\nC. Excision Benign Lesion & MarginsClinical Diagnosis: CystLocation: Mid Back\nLesion Size: 1.8 - 1.5 cm\nExcision Size, including margins: 3.0 x 1.8 cm\nThe patient was evaluated preoperative and noted to be in stable condition. \n Informed consent was obtained from the patient. All risks, benefits, and alternatives regarding the survey have been reviewed in detail with the patient. \n This includes risks of bleeding, infection, scarring recurrence of lesion and need for further procedures. \nAfter consent was obtained, attention was turned toward the area of interest which was disinfected and cleaned with alcohol. Local anesthetic, 1% lidocaine with epinephrine was infiltrated around the site. An elliptical incision with the appropriate margins was made using a Number 15. Dissection of the surrounding/overlying tissue was performed to isolate, expose and remove the lesion. The specimen was placed in a bottle labeled C. #WC20-846. \nThe patient tolerated the procedure well with no complications and minimal bleeding.\n bacitracin was applied at the wound site and covered with a press dressing. Wound care instructions reviewed and given to the patient.\nRepair: Layered Closure \nThe wound was closed with an intermediate layered closure on 06-26-2020. The wound involved the dermis and subcutaneous tissue which required a layer repair to minimize tension and promote optimal healing. The closure was performed in two layers; the deep dermis/ subcutaneous layer was approximated utilizing \nThis layered closure was necessary due to the wounds depth and tissue separation. The location of the wound required reinforcement with a deep dermal closure to prevent breakdown and minimize risk of wound complications. The final closure size is 3.0 cm. \nPressure was applied to achieve hemostasis. Bacitracin was applied at the wound site and it was bandaged. Patient tolerated the procedure well and wound care instructions were reviewed and given to the patient.'}]
